    "title": "Pager or editor shell escape (GTFOBin)",
    "desc": "A pager or editor was driven non-interactively into running a shell command - vim/nvim/view with a -c or --cmd script carrying a :! shell escape, :shell, or an embedded :lua/:python/:perl, or ed in script mode with a bang line. This is the GTFOBins pager/editor break-out (MITRE T1202 Indirect Command Execution / T1059): a tool meant to view or edit a file is used to execute code. The interactive form (open vim, type :!sh) shows up as a parent/child shell and is caught by gtfobin_shell_spawn; this rule catches the scripted form, which has no shell child to key on - the escape lives entirely in the editor's own argv.",
